    "c2": {
      "anchor": "o5",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "A page: its jobs, then its mockup",
      "excerpt": "A page: its jobs, then its mockup",
      "text": "the jobs bit should persist.  Should optionall express of the \"jobs\" as Agile Stories",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T17:44:03.680Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:24.211Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  a page's jobs are saved with it for good, into the real site, and each may be written as an Agile story (\"As a ..., I want ..., so that ...\"), with its \"done when\" checks under it (Overview 1.5, marked).  It becomes its own phase, Page Jobs.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:10.312Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "p-site-file#field-3",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Site File",
      "excerpt": "The sitemap is a Spell file the language reads : a link to a page that's gone, o",
      "text": "Let's use the star wars site as an example as well as spellUI",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T21:53:50.597Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "The example site is Spell UI's",
      "offset": 576,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T21:54:48.689Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:03:04.964Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P1's plan:  a second example site from the start, a small Star Wars site (films, people, planets, a <code>:film</code> and a <code>:person</code> page, a settings dialog, a person sidebar), beside Spell UI's.  The click-through phase builds its mockups on it.</p>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:17:42.413Z",
          "text": "Go ahead and model the entire star wars site as it stands"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:18:36.328Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P1's plan, and passed to the agent building it now:  the whole Star Wars example as a site, a list page and a detail page for every collection it has, a settings dialog and a person sidebar.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c10": {
      "anchor": "p-ui-diagram#field-4",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "UI Diagram",
      "excerpt": "Share first: the tree diagram's box measuring (TreeMeasure ) and its line drawin",
      "text": "Also want `movable`",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T22:15:20.961Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Share first",
      "offset": 0,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T22:15:26.572Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:18:37.133Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P9's plan:  <code>movable</code> beside <code>resizable</code>, generic too:  drag an element to a new place inside its container (<code>movable=\"horizontally\"</code> / <code>\"vertically\"</code> for one axis), its place remembered;  the diagram's boxes are movable boxes.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c11": {
      "anchor": "p-pages-by-address#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Pages By Address",
      "excerpt": "Open the example site in Run: its first page shows; change the address to /butto",
      "text": "\"Not Found page\" should automatically be part of every site (although it can be deleted).  Also an \"Error Page\"",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T22:16:12.007Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "no such page",
      "offset": 450,
      "edited": "2026-11-07T22:16:34.623Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T22:18:37.960Z",
          "html": "<p>Folded into P2's plan:  every site has a Not Found page and an Error page from the start, listed in the site file and deletable (a site that deletes one gets a plain built-in one).  The Error page shows when a page fails to draw or load, with the details while designing and a plain apology for a visitor.</p>"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
